00:05:09.700 --> 00:05:09.740
{=11}So

00:05:10.080 --> 00:05:12.710
their respective rulers are surely uneasy.

00:05:14.920 --> 00:05:18.300
Perhaps they are <i>not </i>pursuing
a prolonged battle.

00:05:20.090 --> 00:05:25.390
Oh? Care to explain, Minister?

00:05:25.390 --> 00:05:31.190
They are attempting to weaken
Chin's army on every battlefield,

00:05:31.190 --> 00:05:34.980
waiting for the opportunity
for an all-out mass attack.

00:05:34.980 --> 00:05:41.110
They don't want a drawn-out battle--
they want the shortest one possible.

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:44.360
The shortest battle possible?

00:05:44.360 --> 00:05:46.370
Almost certainly.

00:05:46.370 --> 00:05:50.750
We'd get no assistance from other units
if the entire army attacked at once.

00:05:50.750 --> 00:05:54.960
Chin's moment of truth is upon us.

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:57.250
When would this be, High Commander?

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:04.890
From where I stand, I cannot say.

00:06:04.890 --> 00:06:06.600
Still...

00:06:06.600 --> 00:06:11.100
The shrewder ones on the ground
should have already picked up on it.

00:06:14.520 --> 00:06:15.690
Shin...

00:06:20.400 --> 00:06:22.860
So it's tomorrow.

00:06:22.860 --> 00:06:25.320
Shin!

00:06:25.320 --> 00:06:28.580
I thought I'd change the bandages
on your arrow wounds.

00:06:30.910 --> 00:06:32.120
Hmm?

00:06:32.120 --> 00:06:35.500
Actually, would you fix me
a little late-night snack?

00:06:35.500 --> 00:06:37.250
What, <i>now</i>?

00:06:37.250 --> 00:06:38.340
Sure.

00:06:38.340 --> 00:06:41.090
Why not? Just throw somethin' together.

00:06:44.470 --> 00:06:46.470
Shin...

00:06:46.470 --> 00:06:49.890
Fine. But it'll be leftovers.

00:06:49.890 --> 00:06:52.600
Sure. Oh, and make enough
for the guys over there.

00:06:52.600 --> 00:06:53.430
Huh?!

00:06:53.430 --> 00:06:54.770
<i>What</i>?!

00:06:55.770 --> 00:06:58.230
"En" "Gi" "So" "Sho" "Kan"

00:07:03.280 --> 00:07:07.610
It seems I didn't have to
call you all here together.

00:07:07.610 --> 00:07:11.740
Then I have only one thing to tell you:

00:07:11.740 --> 00:07:16.330
Tomorrow night we shall toast
our victory from atop Kankoku Pass!

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:25.340
The Battle of Kankoku Pass

00:07:18.660 --> 00:07:25.340
Day 2

00:07:19.460 --> 00:07:25.260
Ka Rin said Kankoku Pass would fall
after ten days of mediocre battles.

00:07:26.050 --> 00:07:28.510
What's going on here, Ri Boku?

00:07:28.510 --> 00:07:30.510
To be precise,

00:07:30.510 --> 00:07:32.850
after a string of mediocre battles,

00:07:32.850 --> 00:07:38.600
the entire army will launch an all-out
attack and take Kankoku Pass.

00:07:38.600 --> 00:07:40.270
So commander Ka Rin

00:07:40.270 --> 00:07:44.780
took seriously the first-day deaths
of two of our generals.

00:07:44.780 --> 00:07:49.160
Losing a leader is worse than
losing thousands of soldiers.

00:07:49.160 --> 00:07:52.120
We must avoid the risk of
losing a commander,

00:07:52.120 --> 00:07:56.710
maintain our main forces, and work
on wearing down the enemy.

00:07:56.710 --> 00:08:02.630
So we prioritize saving our destructive
power for the final showdown.

00:08:02.630 --> 00:08:06.670
But the coalition army has to worry
about Se breathing down their necks.

00:08:06.670 --> 00:08:10.760
Exactly right. Which is why...

00:08:10.760 --> 00:08:12.510
...it all comes down to timing.

00:08:17.100 --> 00:08:18.850
Timing, huh?

00:08:22.940 --> 00:08:25.440
The weakening of the Chin army,

00:08:25.440 --> 00:08:29.950
counting days from the storming of Kankoku
Pass to estimate the fall of Kanyou,

00:08:29.950 --> 00:08:32.450
the danger of the battle dragging on...

00:08:32.450 --> 00:08:38.210
I've accounted for them all in calculating
the right time to begin the final battle.

00:08:38.210 --> 00:08:41.580
And that time is today: Day 15.

00:08:43.630 --> 00:08:47.460
I knew Ka Rin's ten days
wouldn't be enough.

00:08:47.460 --> 00:08:49.970
All armies, move out!

00:08:49.970 --> 00:08:52.260
All right; let's do this.

00:08:52.260 --> 00:08:54.140
Kan Mei Army, moving out!

