00:09:05.980 --> 00:09:07.480
Here we go.

00:09:08.860 --> 00:09:11.110
You're not getting through!

00:09:12.530 --> 00:09:13.530
Let's go!

00:09:15.330 --> 00:09:18.450
Send Kou Son Ryuu's and
Ri Haku's armies to meet them.

00:09:18.070 --> 00:09:22.120
"Sho"

00:09:18.450 --> 00:09:21.120
The main army will watch
for a chance to kill Lord Hyou.

00:09:21.120 --> 00:09:22.040
Sir!

00:09:22.120 --> 00:09:25.080
Sho Army 
vs. 
Lord Hyou's Army

00:09:25.000 --> 00:09:26.000
Mow them down!

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:27.590
Go, go, go!

00:09:34.800 --> 00:09:37.260
Get in there, Hi Shin Force!

00:09:37.550 --> 00:09:41.560
Ou Sen's Army 
vs. 
En Army

00:09:41.730 --> 00:09:45.400
Don't hold back.
Attack from every route there is!

00:09:45.480 --> 00:09:47.440
"Chin" "Ou"

00:09:46.900 --> 00:09:47.900
Sir!

00:09:47.900 --> 00:09:50.740
The left side is already
requesting reinforcements!

00:09:53.490 --> 00:09:56.830
On the right--is that... Kankoku Pass, sir?

00:09:56.830 --> 00:09:58.160
No.

00:09:57.530 --> 00:10:00.410
So Army 
vs. Mou Bu's
& Tou's Allied Army

00:09:58.160 --> 00:09:59.830
Beyond it.

00:10:00.910 --> 00:10:05.420
Th-The great So commander
Kan Mei's main forces!

00:10:05.420 --> 00:10:08.960
With the second army,
that's 120,000 troops!

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:11.840
"Heki"

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:11.840
Our turn at last, eh, sir?

00:10:11.840 --> 00:10:13.720
That's right.

00:10:11.880 --> 00:10:16.840
Mou Bu's Army
Brigade Commander Heki

00:10:13.720 --> 00:10:16.550
This is our most crucial fight.

00:10:16.550 --> 00:10:21.390
Shou Bun Kun told me
before I left Kanyou...

00:10:21.390 --> 00:10:24.350
If they break through Mou Bu's line,

00:10:24.350 --> 00:10:28.730
the enemy can move along the mountains
to take Kankoku Pass from the side.

00:10:28.730 --> 00:10:33.610
Whereas if we break through
the So army, we'll circle left

00:10:33.610 --> 00:10:40.240
and destroy the flanks of the Gi and
Kan armies as they storm Kankoku Pass.

00:10:40.240 --> 00:10:43.580
Be careful, Heki.

00:10:43.580 --> 00:10:47.840
This battlefield holds
the key to the entire war.

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:49.380
And yet...

00:10:49.380 --> 00:10:54.050
Unbelievably enough,
we have no strategy--not a one!

00:10:56.010 --> 00:11:00.970
Follow my orders and fight
with all your might! That is all.

00:11:00.970 --> 00:11:02.310
Dismissed!

00:11:02.310 --> 00:11:03.310
Huh?

00:11:04.480 --> 00:11:09.110
What on earth are you thinking,
General Mou Bu?

00:11:09.110 --> 00:11:14.190
Mou Bu's Army Brigade

00:11:09.110 --> 00:11:14.110
I've got a bad feeling about this.
Better than Lord Hyou? Really?

00:11:14.190 --> 00:11:17.030
Tou's Army Regiment

00:11:15.700 --> 00:11:16.950
Not yet, sir?

00:11:16.950 --> 00:11:19.450
Father...

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:19.530
Tou's Army Battalion

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:23.410
"Chin" "Mou"

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:44.350
I am Mou Bu, the Middle
Kingdom's mightiest man!

00:11:46.060 --> 00:11:48.150
What the hell?!

00:11:48.150 --> 00:11:53.650
There is no one under
the sun who can stop me!

00:11:55.780 --> 00:11:59.530
So general Kan Mei!

00:11:58.150 --> 00:11:59.610
"So"

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:04.620
I, Mou Bu,

00:12:04.620 --> 00:12:09.460
will crush your head by my own hand!

00:12:15.010 --> 00:12:21.470
The mightiest man leads
the mightiest army!

00:12:21.470 --> 00:12:26.640
The Mou Bu Army is invincible!

00:12:27.550 --> 00:12:33.230
Ryuu Koku

00:12:27.550 --> 00:12:33.230
Roku O Mi

00:12:28.310 --> 00:12:31.440
Hmph. Still with the same old Bayou act.

00:12:31.440 --> 00:12:33.690
No, this is good.

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:38.900
What heat... what an explosion of morale!

00:12:38.900 --> 00:12:44.240
He's set his entire army aflame speaking
almost entirely of himself!

00:12:44.240 --> 00:12:48.410
This--<i>this </i>is Mou Bu!

00:12:48.410 --> 00:12:52.380
Now we charge! First, the left!

00:12:52.380 --> 00:12:53.500
Left army!

00:12:55.250 --> 00:12:56.800
The... the left army?

00:12:56.800 --> 00:12:58.470
The left army?

00:12:58.470 --> 00:13:00.630
Charge!

00:13:00.630 --> 00:13:02.890
That's <i>me</i>!

00:13:02.890 --> 00:13:04.390
L-Let's go!

00:13:13.310 --> 00:13:16.230
I can't believe he's starting with <i>me</i>!

00:13:16.230 --> 00:13:21.660
<i>And </i>sending only 3,000 troops up
against Kan Mei's 60,000!

00:13:21.660 --> 00:13:26.080
H-How should we fight?
I haven't heard anything!

00:13:26.080 --> 00:13:29.540
Calm down. I'm the captain--
I must keep my composure!

00:13:33.250 --> 00:13:36.250
Stay cool... see what the enemy's doing...

00:13:36.250 --> 00:13:37.420
Arrows!

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:39.340
And spears in the front row.

00:13:39.340 --> 00:13:42.510
Which means...
they're poised to intercept us!

00:13:42.510 --> 00:13:44.640
Heki, sir! Move to the back!

00:13:44.640 --> 00:13:47.260
All we can do here is rush forward!

00:13:47.260 --> 00:13:50.020
Stay strong! Onward!

00:13:50.770 --> 00:13:55.690
The cavalry's morale is high.
What about the infantry?

00:13:55.690 --> 00:13:57.780
Good. We'll be fine!

00:13:57.780 --> 00:14:00.070
Here they come!

00:14:00.070 --> 00:14:02.950
No fancy tricks necessary. We'll just...

00:14:04.780 --> 00:14:06.530
...muscle our way through!

00:14:07.830 --> 00:14:08.950
Kill 'em!

00:14:13.250 --> 00:14:15.500
My glaive is cutting well!

00:14:15.500 --> 00:14:20.090
I've been swept up in Mou Bu's
speech with the rest of the men!

00:14:21.510 --> 00:14:24.260
All troops! Keep on going!

00:14:25.550 --> 00:14:29.350
To be struggling so
against a simple charge...

00:14:26.720 --> 00:14:32.680
Kan Mei's Army Tactician

00:14:29.350 --> 00:14:32.600
What on earth is the
right army playing at?

00:14:32.680 --> 00:14:35.270
Kan Mei's Army Tactician & General

00:14:32.940 --> 00:14:36.060
No, the enemy is fighting well.

00:14:36.060 --> 00:14:39.690
Battling on the momentum of
Mou Bu's speech is enough.

00:14:39.690 --> 00:14:42.990
We won't be able to touch
them for a while yet.

00:14:42.990 --> 00:14:46.910
And? What can they hope to
accomplish with 3,000?

00:14:46.910 --> 00:14:49.240
Especially all the way out there?

00:14:48.740 --> 00:14:56.250
Kan Mei's Army Tactician & General

00:14:49.240 --> 00:14:52.700
Indeed. There's no telling
what they're thinking.

00:14:52.700 --> 00:14:56.460
Mou Bu must have ordered an all-out rush.

00:14:56.460 --> 00:15:03.420
With this power difference, Mou Bu
should have led an all-army charge.

00:15:03.420 --> 00:15:07.510
To think he was so foolish as to rush
into a surprise attack doomed to fail.

00:15:07.510 --> 00:15:11.560
He's such a great general--
I'd been looking forward to this.

00:15:11.560 --> 00:15:16.520
From the looks of it, I shouldn't
expect much. Right, Kan Mei?

00:15:23.110 --> 00:15:25.030
Is it time yet, sir?

00:15:25.030 --> 00:15:26.780
The left army's fighting it out alone!

00:15:26.780 --> 00:15:28.620
Send us in, quickly!

00:15:28.620 --> 00:15:33.370
Not yet! Our general has
issued no command!

00:15:33.370 --> 00:15:39.040
Why no action, Mou Bu?
Shouldn't we strike while morale is high?

00:15:39.040 --> 00:15:44.340
I'd heard he was different, but why
rile everyone up for nothing?

00:15:46.300 --> 00:15:50.800
"Gaku"

00:15:46.720 --> 00:15:49.850
Wh-What are you doing, Father?

00:15:53.930 --> 00:15:55.890
Wait... no way...

00:16:00.110 --> 00:16:01.320
Why, you--

00:16:03.230 --> 00:16:04.820
Heki, sir!

00:16:04.820 --> 00:16:06.280
I'm fine!

00:16:06.280 --> 00:16:10.660
Hey, there aren't any troops
following us! Isn't that strange?

00:16:10.660 --> 00:16:15.160
Wait--don't tell me our general
just used us to test the waters!

00:16:17.000 --> 00:16:20.790
How can you not trust
your very own general?!

00:16:20.790 --> 00:16:24.380
Mou Bu is more particular
about victory than anyone.

00:16:24.380 --> 00:16:28.720
I, for one, believe in our general!

00:16:28.720 --> 00:16:30.300
What an eyesore.

00:16:30.300 --> 00:16:35.310
Send 5,000 to the right
and slaughter all oncoming troops!

00:16:35.310 --> 00:16:36.930
Look at that!

00:16:36.930 --> 00:16:39.350
A dust cloud, heading toward
the left army!

00:16:39.350 --> 00:16:42.400
The enemy may have sent
reinforcements to the left!

00:16:47.400 --> 00:16:52.150
"Tou"

00:16:47.570 --> 00:16:52.740
Still no action?! At this rate,
our first left army will die for nothing!

00:16:52.740 --> 00:16:55.290
No! Was that all on a whim?

00:17:07.340 --> 00:17:08.760
All right:

00:17:08.760 --> 00:17:10.840
Starting from the left...

00:17:10.840 --> 00:17:13.260
Charge!

00:17:13.260 --> 00:17:15.010
What?!

00:17:15.010 --> 00:17:16.640
You got it, sir!

00:17:16.640 --> 00:17:18.430
Charge!

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:19.440
Huh?

00:17:21.690 --> 00:17:23.770
<i>Here </i>they come. Finally.

00:17:23.770 --> 00:17:24.770
Hmm?

00:17:28.530 --> 00:17:32.660
Just a moment!
Look at the <i>shape </i>of this charge!

00:17:32.660 --> 00:17:33.660
That's...

00:17:34.990 --> 00:17:36.450
...an echelon sweep!

00:17:38.080 --> 00:17:40.710
An echelon sweep...

00:17:40.710 --> 00:17:42.250
An echelon sweep?

00:17:42.250 --> 00:17:43.670
No doubt about it.

00:17:43.670 --> 00:17:48.130
But... but isn't that an extremely
high-level strategy?

00:17:48.130 --> 00:17:49.260
Sure is.

00:17:49.260 --> 00:17:52.680
Not even the very best tacticians would
think of using an echelon sweep--

00:17:52.680 --> 00:17:55.430
not in a battle of this scale!

00:17:59.430 --> 00:18:02.520
Has that man gone mad?

00:18:02.520 --> 00:18:07.230
Does he mean to challenge <i>us</i>,
the So army, to a battle of tactics?

00:18:12.030 --> 00:18:16.700
Applying an echelon sweep puts
diagonal force along the line.

00:18:12.730 --> 00:18:20.950
Line-abreast

00:18:12.730 --> 00:18:20.950
Echelon

00:18:16.700 --> 00:18:20.870
This force moves like a wave, causing
minute disturbances in the formation.

00:18:21.370 --> 00:18:26.340
But even small disturbances in the
formation lead to scattered focus...

00:18:28.210 --> 00:18:30.630
Cue the enemy, charging front and center.

00:18:33.300 --> 00:18:36.680
But this creates yet
another diagonal wave.

00:18:36.680 --> 00:18:39.930
If this wave goes on uninterrupted
for strike after strike,

00:18:39.930 --> 00:18:43.270
the echelon sweep can have a huge impact.

00:18:43.270 --> 00:18:49.150
In theory, anyway. In reality,
it's considered impractical.

00:18:49.150 --> 00:18:55.990
B-But... Mou Bu's echelon looks
to be a resounding success.

00:18:57.070 --> 00:19:02.040
Young master... Forgive me,
but is that <i>really </i>Mou Bu?

00:19:03.040 --> 00:19:05.540
Wow, Pops. Rude.

00:19:05.540 --> 00:19:07.210
Apologies.

00:19:07.210 --> 00:19:09.920
But it's surprising, all right.

00:19:09.920 --> 00:19:14.680
My tactics-despising father whips
out a whole strategy--

00:19:14.680 --> 00:19:18.140
and what is it but this
super-sophisticated play!

00:19:18.140 --> 00:19:19.140
Sir!

00:19:20.720 --> 00:19:23.520
Rai Ki's at the right edge--
he's moving out!

00:19:23.520 --> 00:19:25.190
I'm counting on you.

00:19:25.190 --> 00:19:27.190
I've got this!

00:19:27.190 --> 00:19:28.810
Charge!

00:19:31.280 --> 00:19:34.320
Now our army's vast size
has backfired on us.

00:19:34.320 --> 00:19:35.700
Indeed.

00:19:35.700 --> 00:19:41.700
The troops had to form rather
dense lines to fit on these plains.

00:19:41.700 --> 00:19:45.960
That made it easier for the diagonal
wave to move through them.

00:19:45.960 --> 00:19:50.630
If he went with this attack
knowing what would happen...

00:19:50.630 --> 00:19:54.090
We must tread lightly or we'll get burned.

00:19:54.090 --> 00:19:58.470
Kan Mei. Please send 5,000
reserves to the left.

00:19:58.470 --> 00:20:02.970
If that echelon is well blended,
the final unit will be the strongest.

00:20:02.970 --> 00:20:07.230
It'll destroy the edges of our formations
and target the back side.

00:20:07.230 --> 00:20:11.110
Your head's too full of
the enemy's schemes!

00:20:12.730 --> 00:20:14.940
It's simple:

00:20:14.940 --> 00:20:21.580
Half of Mou Bu's men have clashed with
half mine--20,000 versus 60.

00:20:21.580 --> 00:20:24.120
If this clever plan has the
main force along the edges,

00:20:24.120 --> 00:20:28.670
then your order of 5,000
reserves is all it'll take.

00:20:28.670 --> 00:20:31.960
Then we just crush any foes
who leap into the fray!

00:20:33.500 --> 00:20:35.380
You are most correct.

00:20:35.380 --> 00:20:39.640
Kan Mei's soldiers! Become as beasts!

00:20:41.100 --> 00:20:44.970
A melee is exactly what you want!

00:20:44.970 --> 00:20:49.480
Show them the sheer terror
of the So army!

00:20:49.480 --> 00:20:54.070
We shall devour fully half
of Mou Bu by noon!

00:20:56.400 --> 00:21:01.410
Ben, sir, Kan Mei's speech has set
the neighboring So army aflame!

00:21:01.410 --> 00:21:02.870
Yes.

00:21:02.870 --> 00:21:07.370
But Mou Bu started that fire.
This is exactly what he wanted.

00:21:07.370 --> 00:21:09.540
It... it is?

00:21:09.540 --> 00:21:12.500
In any case, now that they've moved in,

00:21:12.500 --> 00:21:15.170
that battlefield will flow with
staggering amounts of blood.

00:21:16.840 --> 00:21:19.010
Ugh, that man-stink.

00:21:19.010 --> 00:21:21.220
What a stench.

00:21:21.220 --> 00:21:24.430
Ka Rin! General Ka Rin!

00:21:24.430 --> 00:21:25.850
Ka Rin, ma'am!

00:21:26.970 --> 00:21:28.930
Adjutant Bam Yu

00:21:27.020 --> 00:21:29.730
--It's all ready to go!
--You're <i>late</i>.

00:21:32.020 --> 00:21:37.150
Guess this means the second army
is finally gonna get to fightin'!

00:21:39.240 --> 00:21:40.990
Get going already!

00:21:43.320 --> 00:21:47.660
The beginning is the thing
when it comes to war.

00:21:47.660 --> 00:21:52.370
They tell you what a given
general considers important.

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:56.340
In my case, that's opulence and dread.

00:21:56.340 --> 00:21:57.670
That, and...

00:21:57.670 --> 00:22:00.220
...just a pinch of cuteness.

00:22:03.050 --> 00:22:06.260
Sir! Ka Rin's army is on the move!

00:22:06.260 --> 00:22:09.140
Put Roku O Mi and Kan Ou in the front.

00:22:11.970 --> 00:22:13.930
Tou's Army Kan Ou

00:22:12.940 --> 00:22:13.940
Hmm?

00:22:18.030 --> 00:22:21.030
A chariot squadron?

00:22:21.030 --> 00:22:26.200
That's odd. The size of the dust cloud
doesn't fit the number of chariots.

00:22:28.540 --> 00:22:29.540
Now!

00:22:34.920 --> 00:22:37.250
They veered sharply to the side!

00:22:37.250 --> 00:22:39.880
They're kicking up dust. A screen?

00:22:39.880 --> 00:22:44.010
Slow your horses! Whoa!

00:22:44.010 --> 00:22:46.100
But whatever for?

00:22:48.680 --> 00:22:50.970
For drama.

00:22:50.970 --> 00:22:51.980
What the--

00:22:53.230 --> 00:22:54.230
Eh?

00:23:10.490 --> 00:23:12.870
What the hell is that?!

00:23:12.870 --> 00:23:15.870
It's those--from the southern lands--

00:23:15.870 --> 00:23:20.130
These are no chariots.
They're war elephants.

00:23:20.130 --> 00:23:21.960
Aren't their eyes <i>adorable</i>?

00:24:52.510 --> 00:25:02.020
A Promotion in a Predicament

00:24:54.220 --> 00:24:58.560
Next time on Kingdom:
"A Promotion in a Predicament."
